# JavaScript only (no TypeScript)

This project is **plain JavaScript**. Do not introduce TypeScript.

## Do not

- Add or use **`.ts`**, **`.tsx`**, **`.mts`**, or **`.cts`** source files.
- Add **`.d.ts`** declaration files (use **`jsconfig.json`** + Vite’s client types for editor hints instead).
- Use **`<script lang="ts">`** or **`lang="tsx"`** in Vue SFCs; use **`<script setup>`** or **`<script>`** with default JS only.
- Add **`tsconfig.json`** or the **`typescript`** npm package unless an upstream tool *requires* it and there is no JS alternative.

## Do

- Write **`.js`** modules and **`.vue`** files with JavaScript `<script>` blocks.
- Use **JSDoc** (`@param`, `@returns`, `@type`, etc.) when extra type clarity helps readers or tooling.

## Examples

```vue
<!-- Bad -->
<script setup lang="ts">
const x: number = 1;
</script>

<!-- Good -->
<script setup>
const x = 1;
</script>
```

```text
Bad:  src/game.ts, src/types.d.ts, tsconfig.json
Good: src/game.js, jsconfig.json (noEmit, allowJs, for editor only)
```
